<!--
    THE EIGHTH DAY - traders.xml
    ===========================

    THE ONE RULE
    ============
    The trader sells INPUTS. It never sells a Calling's OUTPUT.

    You can buy flux, reagent base, seeds, precision parts and polymer, because
    those are the raw end of chains anyone can run. You can never buy hardened
    steel, carbide, composite plate, a serum, a shaped charge or any weapon,
    because those are what a Calling is FOR. A Calling whose product is on a
    shelf is a Calling nobody needs.

    This is enforced mechanically, not by care: tools/check-unlocks.py fails the
    build if any perk-gated item appears in trader stock. Adding one is a
    deliberate act, not an accident.

    Field Notes are excluded for the same reason. The research loop's whole
    premise is that you cannot buy your way past it - see items.xml.

    STOCK FOLLOWS THE TURNING
    =========================
    DESIGN.md promises that trader stock "rotates toward things you now need
    instead of things you wanted". Three tiers deliver that, and the shift is
    deliberate:

      Foundation  bootstrapping. Seeds, compost, first metal. You are BUILDING.
      Industry    the middle. Parts, polymer, reagents, oil. You are SCALING.
      Attrition   the late game. Medical stock, alcohol, powder, rations.
                  You are not building any more. You are SUSTAINING.

    By Cycle 5 a player is not shopping for a new workshop, they are shopping to
    stay alive, and the shelf should say so.

    VERIFY-23 (docs/VERIFICATION.md): the tier attribute below is the intended
    gate. If V3.2 does not gate trader stock this way, all three tiers are simply
    available from the start - more stock than intended, which is a balance
    problem rather than a break. Confirm how vanilla tiers its own groups.
-->
<configs>

    <!-- ==========================================================================
         CALLING WRITS - NO LONGER SOLD

         0.1 sold Writs here as a placeholder so the Calling system could be
         tested before the Proving chains existed. The Provings landed in 0.2
         (see quests.xml), so the stock is gone and a Writ is now obtainable
         only by completing a Proving.

         This is deliberate and load-bearing: a Calling that can be bought is a
         purchase, and the entire pillar rests on it being work. Do not add
         Writs back to trader stock, to loot, or to any recipe.
         ========================================================================== -->


    <!-- ==========================================================================
         FOUNDATION - you are building

         The bootstrap tier. Seeds matter most here: without them the farm
         cannot start, because a seed recipe needs a crop and a crop needs a
         seed. This shelf is the only thing that breaks that circle.
         ========================================================================== -->

    <append xpath="/traders/trader_items">

        <trader_item_group name="edStockFoundation">
            <item name="edSeedFlax" count="2,5" />
            <item name="edSeedRye" count="2,5" />
            <item name="edSeedComfrey" count="1,3" />
            <item name="edSeedRapeseed" count="1,3" />
            <item name="edResourceFertiliser" count="4,10" />
            <item name="edResourceFlux" count="10,25" />
            <item name="edResourceCrudeIron" count="5,15" />
        </trader_item_group>

    </append>


    <!-- ==========================================================================
         INDUSTRY - you are scaling

         The chokepoints, in small quantities at bad prices. This shelf exists to
         unblock a player whose chain has stalled on one missing input - never to
         replace the chain. Quantities stay low for exactly that reason.
         ========================================================================== -->

    <append xpath="/traders/trader_items">

        <trader_item_group name="edStockIndustry">
            <item name="edResourcePrecisionParts" count="1,3" />
            <item name="edResourcePolymer" count="2,6" />
            <item name="edResourceReagentBase" count="2,6" />
            <item name="edResourceLinseedOil" count="2,5" />
            <item name="edResourceRyeFlour" count="3,8" />
        </trader_item_group>

    </append>


    <!-- ==========================================================================
         ATTRITION - you are sustaining

         Late stock. Note what is NOT here: no new workshop materials, no gear.
         By Cycle 5 the question stopped being "what can I build" and became
         "can I keep going", and the shelf answers the second question.

         Reagent base in quantity because the Apothecary is burning through it.
         Powder because the Marshal is. Rations because nobody is farming while
         the Hollow is out.
         ========================================================================== -->

    <append xpath="/traders/trader_items">

        <trader_item_group name="edStockAttrition">
            <item name="edResourceReagentBase" count="5,12" />
            <item name="edResourceCrudeAlcohol" count="2,6" />
            <item name="edFoodHardtack" count="2,6" />
            <item name="edFoodBoneBroth" count="2,5" />
            <item name="resourceGunPowder" count="20,60" />
            <item name="resourceCloth" count="10,30" />
        </trader_item_group>

    </append>


    <!-- ==========================================================================
         STOCKING THE TRADERS

         *** THIS IS THE PATCH THAT WAS MISSING. ***

         Until 0.6 the groups above were defined and referenced by nothing, so
         every one of them was unbuyable - including the seeds, which meant the
         farm could not be bootstrapped at all except through a 4% loot roll.

         Defining a trader_item_group does not put it on a shelf. Something has
         to stock it. check-refs.py now treats an unstocked group as an orphan so
         this cannot happen again.

         Appending to /traders/trader_info/items hits every trader in the game.
         ========================================================================== -->

    <append xpath="/traders/trader_info/items">
        <item_group name="edStockFoundation" count="2,4" tier="1,5" />
        <item_group name="edStockIndustry" count="1,3" tier="2,5" />
        <item_group name="edStockAttrition" count="2,4" tier="3,5" />
    </append>

</configs>
